      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.19,
          "end": 7.41,
          "en": "Now, just to finish this up, this modal here and to practice events again, let's make sure we can",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 7.41,
          "end": 9.99,
          "en": "actually close the modal because right now we can't.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 10.17,
          "end": 14.82,
          "en": "And for that, we also might want to have a way of showing the modal in the first place.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 14.82,
          "end": 22.14,
          "en": "So for that, I'll add a button here in the app svelte file and let's add a new variable in here, a",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 22.14,
          "end": 26.51,
          "en": "normal variable which could be show modal, which by default is false.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 26.52,
          "end": 32.52,
          "en": "And when we click this button here, so on a click, I want to set show modal to true and here because",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 32.52,
          "end": 36.42,
          "en": "I'm lazy, I'll just use the inline version and set show modal to true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 36.45,
          "end": 42.96,
          "en": "Now with that, all we have to do is wrap that modal in a if check and only if show modal is true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 43.41,
          "end": 46.44,
          "en": "Only then this will be added to the dom.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 46.47,
          "end": 47.91,
          "en": "Otherwise it's not added.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 47.91,
          "end": 50.94,
          "en": "It's a regular svelte if block.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 51.09,
          "end": 52.14,
          "en": "So now we don't see it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 52.14,
          "end": 53.97,
          "en": "But if I click show modal, here it is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 54.24,
          "end": 55.38,
          "en": "Now we want to close it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 55.38,
          "end": 60.36,
          "en": "When I click the backdrop or when I click the confirm or the default close button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 60.78,
          "end": 63.91,
          "en": "Now let's start with the backdrop and the default close button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 63.91,
          "end": 65.05,
          "en": "For this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 65.05,
          "end": 66.46,
          "en": "I want to emit my own event.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 66.46,
          "end": 69.03999999999999,
          "en": "I want to emit my own cancel event.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 69.67,
          "end": 70.93,
          "en": "So let's go here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 70.93,
          "end": 80.74,
          "en": "Let's import create event dispatcher to practice this again from Svelte, let's create a dispatch constant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 80.74,
          "end": 82.87,
          "en": "and store this event.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 82.87,
          "end": 84.46000000000001,
          "en": "Dispatcher function in it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 84.61,
          "end": 86.8,
          "en": "And then here when we click the backdrop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 87.53999999999999,
          "end": 88.71000000000001,
          "en": "We can.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 90.38,
          "end": 91.76,
          "en": "Emit our own event.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 92.64,
          "end": 97.35,
          "en": "By calling dispatch and maybe name this cancel because we clicked the backdrop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 97.35,
          "end": 100.32,
          "en": "And then let's say maybe it matters to our application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 100.32,
          "end": 105.84,
          "en": "When we click the button, we also emit our own custom event, but it's not called cancel, but it's",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 105.84,
          "end": 109.59,
          "en": "called close because maybe closing is different than canceling in the app here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 109.59,
          "end": 111.9,
          "en": "It isn't, but of course it could be in your app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 111.9,
          "end": 115.11,
          "en": "So here I'm emitting close the close event up there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 115.11,
          "end": 118.59,
          "en": "I'm emitting cancel now in app svelte.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 118.68,
          "end": 124.23,
          "en": "We now just have to listen to that on the modal component here we can listen to on cancel.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 124.76,
          "end": 128.09,
          "en": "And we can listen to on close because we're emitting these two events.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 128.18,
          "end": 132.35,
          "en": "Now, of course, here I want to do the same thing on both events, but that's just how it is in this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 132.35,
          "end": 132.8,
          "en": "app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 132.8,
          "end": 135.95,
          "en": "So in both cases I want to set show modal to false.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 137.86,
          "end": 140.41,
          "en": "Do that here as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 141.7,
          "end": 145.75,
          "en": "And when we click this confirm button here, well, I want to do exactly the same.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 145.75,
          "end": 149.95,
          "en": "So here it's a normal on click listener because this is a normal button on which I'm registering it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 149.98,
          "end": 151.36,
          "en": "That's also important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 151.39,
          "end": 157.84,
          "en": "Just because you're passing this content into the slot of another component does not mean that you can",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 157.84,
          "end": 160.32999999999998,
          "en": "only interact with it from inside this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 160.32999999999998,
          "end": 162.37,
          "en": "Indeed, you can't easily do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 162.37,
          "end": 167.92000000000002,
          "en": "Instead, here you still interact from inside the component where the markup is defined, even if it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 167.92000000000002,
          "end": 170.82999999999998,
          "en": "then technically is passed into another component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 170.82999999999998,
          "end": 178.39,
          "en": "So here I still set up my click listener there and pass in exactly the same function code as I have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 178.39,
          "end": 179.17000000000002,
          "en": "up there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 179.17000000000002,
          "end": 185.62,
          "en": "So now if we do that show modal, click the backdrop and close it, click confirm and close it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 185.62,
          "end": 191.38,
          "en": "And in case we would not provide our button here, the default should be shown the default close button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 191.38,
          "end": 193.24,
          "en": "and that also closes the modal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 193.24,
          "end": 195.67,
          "en": "So opening and closing, that works.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
